{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778376977483,"sessionID":"ses_1f079647cffeDkFvZKT68tb1VL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_bPfa2DDh7YxHEdqhV3Mb21c1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"obo-grep.pl --noheader -r 'id: MONDO:777' src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo","timeout":120000,"workdir":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo","description":"Checks temporary MONDO ID clashes"},"output":"[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770001\nname: equine juvenile spinocerebellar ataxia, FDXR-related, horse\ndef: \"Any spinocerebellar ataxia that occurs in horses due to a variation in the FDXR gene. EJSCA is a degenerative axonopathy characterized by acute onset of ataxia within the first month of life, affecting the pelvic limbs more severely than the thoracic limb and rapidly progressing to inability to stand.\" [doi:10.1016/j.jevs.2025.105561, PMID:38669583]\nsynonym: \"EJSCA\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:38669583]\nis_a: MONDO:1012960 {source=\"PMID:38669583\"} ! hereditary cerebellar ataxia, non-human animal\nintersection_of: MONDO:1012960 ! hereditary cerebellar ataxia, non-human animal\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/100060312 ! FDXR\nintersection_of: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9796 ! Equus caballus\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/100060312 {source=\"PMID:38669583\"} ! FDXR\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9796 {source=\"PMID:38669583\"} ! Equus caballus\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9143\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770002\nname: avoidant/restrictive food intake disorder\ndef: \"An eating disorder characterized by avoidance or restriction of food intake due to one or more of the following: lack of interest in eating or food, sensitivity to sensory characteristics of food (such as taste, texture, smell, or appearance), or concern about aversive consequences of eating (such as choking or vomiting), resulting in persistent failure to meet appropriate nutritional and/or energy needs as manifested by significant weight loss, nutritional deficiency, dependence on enteral feeding or nutritional supplements, or marked interference with psychosocial functioning, and where the eating disturbance is not better explained by lack of available food, cultural or religious practices, another mental disorder, or a concurrent medical condition.\" [PMID:38849953]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0051057\"}\nsynonym: \"ARFID\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [DOID:0051057, PMID:38849953]\nsynonym: \"selective eating disorder\" EXACT [PMID:38849953]\nxref: DOID:0051057 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: ICD10CM:F50.82 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: ICD9:307.59 {source=\"MONDO:relatedTo\"}\nxref: MESH:D000080146 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005451 {source=\"PMID:38849953\"} ! eating disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3311-7320\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9408\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770003\nname: cystic fibrosis-related diabetes\ndef: \"A form of diabetes mellitus unique to individuals with cystic fibrosis (CF), arising primarily from progressive fibrotic destruction of the pancreas leading to insulin deficiency, with additional contributions from insulin resistance. CFRD affects approximately 20% of adolescents and 40-50% of adults with CF. It shares features with both type 1 and type 2 diabetes but is a distinct clinical entity with its own diagnostic criteria and management guidelines.\" [PMID:21115772, PMID:29515516]\nsynonym: \"CF-related diabetes\" EXACT [PMID:21115772]\nsynonym: \"CFRD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:21115772]\nxref: ICD10CM:E13 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005015 {source=\"PMID:21115772\"} ! diabetes mellitus\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005015 ! diabetes mellitus\nintersection_of: disease_arises_from_feature MONDO:0009061 ! cystic fibrosis\nrelationship: disease_arises_from_feature MONDO:0009061 {source=\"PMID:21115772\"} ! cystic fibrosis\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770004\nname: CFTR-related disorder\ndef: \"A disease associated with CFTR (cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator) dysfunction that does not fulfill the diagnostic criteria for cystic fibrosis (CF). CFTR-related disorders are characterized by clinical evidence of CFTR dysfunction limited to a single organ system, a sweat chloride concentration below the CF diagnostic threshold (typically less than 60 mmol/L), and CFTR genotypes that often include at least one variant not classified as CF-causing. Recognized CFTR-related disorders include congenital bilateral absence of the vas deferens (CBAVD), acute recurrent or chronic pancreatitis, and disseminated bronchiectasis.\" [PMID:20301428, PMID:21658649]\ncomment: A CFTR-related disorder is defined as a clinical entity with evidence of CFTR dysfunction in at least one organ system that **does not meet** the diagnostic criteria for CF. Typically this means:\\n- Sweat chloride below the CF diagnostic threshold (<60 mmol/L)\\n- Clinical involvement limited to a single organ system\\n- CFTR genotype that includes at least one variant not classified as CF-causing\\n\\nSee 'cystic fibrosis' (MONDO:0009061) for diagnosis criteria for CF.\nsynonym: \"CFTR-RD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:21658649]\nsynonym: \"CFTR-related disease\" RELATED [PMID:21658649]\nxref: MEDGEN:1854862 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5924204 {source=\"MEDGEN:1854862\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"PMID:21658649\"} ! hereditary disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1884 {source=\"PMID:21658649\"} ! CFTR\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770005\nname: cystic fibrosis-related liver disease\ndef: \"A liver disorder that arises as a consequence of cystic fibrosis. Cystic fibrosis-related liver disease encompasses a spectrum of hepatobiliary abnormalities caused by CFTR dysfunction in cholangiocytes, including focal biliary cirrhosis, multilobular biliary cirrhosis, hepatic steatosis, and cholangiopathy. It is a significant cause of non-pulmonary morbidity and mortality in CF, affecting approximately 5-10% of CF patients.\" [PMID:28753176, PMID:37278811]\nsynonym: \"CF liver disease\" EXACT [PMID:28753176]\nsynonym: \"CF-related liver disease\" EXACT [PMID:28753176]\nsynonym: \"CFLD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:28753176]\nis_a: MONDO:0005154 {source=\"PMID:28753176\"} ! liver disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005154 ! liver disorder\nintersection_of: disease_arises_from_feature MONDO:0009061 ! cystic fibrosis\nrelationship: disease_arises_from_feature MONDO:0009061 {source=\"PMID:28753176\"} ! cystic fibrosis\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770006\nname: disease by body system or component\ndef: \"A grouping class for human diseases classified by the body system or anatomical component primarily affected.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2360-2664]\ncomment: This term is intended solely for classification purposes and should not be used for direct data annotation.\nis_a: MONDO:0700096 ! human disease\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770007\nname: disease by developmental or physiological process\ndef: \"A grouping class for human diseases classified by the molecular, biochemical, cellular, anatomic, developmental or physiological process that is disrupted.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2360-2664]\ncomment: This term is intended solely for classification purposes and should not be used for direct data annotation.\nis_a: MONDO:0700096 ! human disease\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770008\nname: disease by etiologic mechanism\ndef: \"A grouping class for human diseases classified by their etiologic mechanism, encompassing primarily intrinsic (genetic, genomic), primarily extrinsic (e.g., infections, toxins, radiation), and complex multifactorial (e.g. nutritional) causes.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2360-2664]\ncomment: This term is intended solely for classification purposes and should not be used for direct data annotation.\nis_a: MONDO:0700096 ! human disease\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770009\nname: disease of genetic or genomic mechanism\ndef: \"A grouping class for human diseases caused by genetic or genomic alterations, including chromosomal abnormalities and heritable mutations.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2360-2664]\ncomment: This term is intended solely for classification purposes and should not be used for direct data annotation.\nis_a: MONDO:7770008 ! disease by etiologic mechanism\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770010\nname: disease of primarily extrinsic mechanism\ndef: \"A grouping class for human diseases caused primarily by extrinsic factors, including infections, toxins, nutritional deficiencies, iatrogenic causes, and environmental exposures.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2360-2664]\ncomment: This term is intended solely for classification purposes and should not be used for direct data annotation.\nis_a: MONDO:7770008 ! disease by etiologic mechanism\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770011\nname: disease by molecular mechanism\ndef: \"A grouping class for human diseases classified by their underlying molecular or pathophysiological mechanism, such as protein aggregation, ion channel dysfunction, or signal transduction disruption.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2360-2664]\ncomment: This term is intended solely for classification purposes and should not be used for direct data annotation.\nis_a: MONDO:0700096 ! human disease\nis_a: MONDO:7770007 ! disease by developmental or physiological process\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770012\nname: disease by body system or component, non-human animal\ndef: \"Disease by body system or component that occurs in non-human animals.\" [MONDO:patterns/nonhuman_disease]\ncomment: This term is intended solely for classification purposes and should not be used for direct data annotation.\nis_a: MONDO:0005583 ! non-human animal disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005583 ! non-human animal disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700097 MONDO:7770006 ! cross-species analog disease by body system or component\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10127\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770013\nname: disease by developmental or physiological process, non-human animal\ndef: \"Disease by developmental or physiological process that occurs in non-human animals.\" [MONDO:patterns/nonhuman_disease]\ncomment: This term is intended solely for classification purposes and should not be used for direct data annotation.\nis_a: MONDO:0005583 ! non-human animal disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005583 ! non-human animal disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700097 MONDO:7770007 ! cross-species analog disease by developmental or physiological process\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10127\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770014\nname: disease by etiologic mechanism, non-human animal\ndef: \"Disease by etiologic mechanism that occurs in non-human animals.\" [MONDO:patterns/nonhuman_disease]\ncomment: This term is intended solely for classification purposes and should not be used for direct data annotation.\nis_a: MONDO:0005583 ! non-human animal disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005583 ! non-human animal disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700097 MONDO:7770008 ! cross-species analog disease by etiologic mechanism\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10127\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770015\nname: disease of genetic or genomic mechanism, non-human animal\ndef: \"Disease of genetic or genomic mechanism that occurs in non-human animals.\" [MONDO:patterns/nonhuman_disease]\ncomment: This term is intended solely for classification purposes and should not be used for direct data annotation.\nis_a: MONDO:0005583 ! non-human animal disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005583 ! non-human animal disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700097 MONDO:7770009 ! cross-species analog disease of genetic or genomic mechanism\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10127\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770016\nname: disease of primarily extrinsic mechanism, non-human animal\ndef: \"Disease of primarily extrinsic mechanism that occurs in non-human animals.\" [MONDO:patterns/nonhuman_disease]\ncomment: This term is intended solely for classification purposes and should not be used for direct data annotation.\nis_a: MONDO:0005583 ! non-human animal disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005583 ! non-human animal disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700097 MONDO:7770010 ! cross-species analog disease of primarily extrinsic mechanism\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10127\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770017\nname: disease by molecular mechanism, non-human animal\ndef: \"Disease by molecular mechanism that occurs in non-human animals.\" [MONDO:patterns/nonhuman_disease]\ncomment: This term is intended solely for classification purposes and should not be used for direct data annotation.\nis_a: MONDO:0005583 ! non-human animal disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005583 ! non-human animal disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700097 MONDO:7770011 ! cross-species analog disease by molecular mechanism\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10127\" xsd:anyURI\n\n","metadata":{"output":"[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770001\nname: equine juvenile spinocerebellar ataxia, FDXR-related, horse\ndef: \"Any spinocerebellar ataxia that occurs in horses due to a variation in the FDXR gene. EJSCA is a degenerative axonopathy characterized by acute onset of ataxia within the first month of life, affecting the pelvic limbs more severely than the thoraci