arch-initiative/mondo/issues/8003\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1030011\nname: paroxysmal atrial fibrillation\ndef: \"An atrial fibrillation disorder characterized by intermittent atrial fibrillation that lasts less than seven days from onset.\" [https://orcid.org/0009-0009-6791-365X, PMID:38033089]\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C80391\"}\nsynonym: \"paroxymsal AFib\" EXACT [NCIT:C80391]\nsynonym: \"paroxysmal AF\" EXACT [NCIT:C80391]\nxref: ICD10CM:I48.0 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: icd11.foundation:542703670 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:115990 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: NCIT:C80391 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: SCTID:282825002 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0235480 {source=\"MEDGEN:115990\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0004981 {source=\"PMID:38033089\", source=\"icd11.foundation:542703670\"} ! atrial fibrillation\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3458-4839\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7886\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060134\nname: atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease\ndef: \"Any cardiovascular disease resulting from atherosclerosis.\" [NCIT:C35771]\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C35771\"}\nxref: NCIT:C35771 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005311 {source=\"NCIT:C35771\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8049-2559\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4593-1186\"} ! atherosclerosis\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9124\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060171\nname: diffuse midline glioma, H3 K27-altered\ndef: \"A diffuse midline glioma characterized by H3 K27 alteration and usually either a histone H3 K27M mutation, an EGFR mutation, or aberrant overexpression of EZHIP. The prognosis is poor.\" [NCIT:C185368]\ncomment: Currently, diffuse midline glioma, H3 K27M-mutant is the single child term. Other child terms will be added during Mondo alignment with NCIT.\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028173\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C185368\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"DMG, H3 K27-altered\" EXACT [PMID:37835563]\nxref: GARD:0028173 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1811313 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: NCIT:C185368 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5669877 {source=\"MEDGEN:1811313\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0006033 {source=\"NCIT:C185368\"} ! diffuse intrinsic pontine glioma\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9513\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060180\nname: brain stem glioblastoma\ndef: \"A glioblastoma localized in the brain stem.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489, NCIT:C5097]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028180\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C5097\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0028180 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:231460 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: NCIT:C5097 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C1332610 {source=\"MEDGEN:231460\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002501 {source=\"NCIT:C5097\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\"} ! brain glioblastoma\nintersection_of: MONDO:0018177 ! glioblastoma\nintersection_of: disease_has_location UBERON:0002298 ! brainstem\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9644\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060188\nname: small plaque parapsoriasis\ndef: \"A variant of parapsoriasis characterized by round-to-oval plaques less than 5cm in diameter, and it rarely progresses.\" [NCIT:C3921, PMID:35426607]\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:3921\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:75515 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: NCIT:3921 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0263370 {source=\"MEDGEN:75515\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0006592 {source=\"NCIT:C3921\"} ! parapsoriasis\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9686\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060189\nname: large plaque parapsoriasis\ndef: \"A variant of parapsoriasis characterized by erythematous-to-brown patches or thin plaques with fine scales larger than 5cm in diameter. It has a substantial risk to evolve to mycosis fungoides.\" [NCIT:C3670, PMID:35426607]\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C3670\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:57907 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: NCIT:C3670 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0162442 {source=\"MEDGEN:57907\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0006592 {source=\"NCIT:C3670\"} ! parapsoriasis\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9686\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:8000010\nname: antiphospholipid syndrome\ndef: \"A disorder caused by the presence of autoantibodies directed against phospholipids, causing a hypercoaguable state, which may result in blood clots, stroke, heart attack, and in women, significant pregnancy-related complications, including miscarriage and still birth. The syndrome is often associated with other autoimmune disorders, most commonly lupus erythematosus, and infections, including syphilis and Lyme disease.\" [NCIT:C61283]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nsubset: doid_rare {source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0005824\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C61283\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:80\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:80\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:80\"}\nsubset: otar {source=\"MONDO:OTAR\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"antiphospholipid antibody syndrome\" EXACT [DOID:2988, ICD10CM:D68.61, NCIT:C61283, Orphanet:80]\nsynonym: \"antiphospholipid syndrome\" EXACT [DOID:2988, ICD10CM:D68.61, icd11.foundation:1173370808, NCIT:C61283, Orphanet:80]\nsynonym: \"familial lupus anticoagulant\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"Hughes syndrome\" EXACT [icd11.foundation:1173370808, Orphanet:80]\nxref: DOID:2988 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: EFO:0002689 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:EFO\"}\nxref: GARD:0005824 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: ICD10CM:D68.61 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nxref: icd11.foundation:1173370808 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"Orphanet:80\"}\nxref: ICD9:279.49 {source=\"MONDO:relatedTo\", source=\"MONDO:i2s\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:38834 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: MESH:D016736 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nxref: NCIT:C61283 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nxref: Orphanet:80 {source=\"OMIM:107320\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: SCTID:19267009 {source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nxref: SCTID:201450008 {source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nxref: SCTID:26843008 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0085278 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:38834\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"NCIT:C61283\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0007179 {source=\"DOID:2988\", source=\"MESH:D016736\"} ! autoimmune disease\nrelationship: disease_has_feature HP:0001977 {source=\"NCIT:C61283\"} ! Abnormal thrombosis\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/antiphospholipid_syndrome\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:8000023\nname: type 3 autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome\ndef: \"A rare, primary immunodeficiency. It is caused by a currently undetermined defect in the Fas-induced apoptosis pathway. No mutations in Fas, FASLG or CASP10 are detectable. Disruption of Fas-induced apoptosis impairs lymphocyte homeostasis and immune tolerance. Characteristic laboratory findings include an increase in circulating, double-negative (CD4-/CD8-) T cells in the setting of immune-mediated anemia, thrombocytopenia and neutropenia. Clinical signs present in childhood include fatigue, pallor, bruising, hepatosplenomegaly and chronic, non-malignant, non-infectious lymphadenopathy. The clinical course is influenced by a strong association with other autoimmune disorders and an increased risk for developing Hodgkin and non-Hodgkin lymphoma.\" [NCIT:C39577]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027040\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C39577\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0027040 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:274327 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: NCIT:C39577 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C1519711 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:274327\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0017979 {source=\"NCIT:C39577\"} ! autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/4098\" xsd:anyURI\n\n","metadata":{"output":"...\n\nDOID:0081253 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: GARD:0026778 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: NCIT:C186351 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0850340 {source=\"DOID:0081253\"} ! supratentorial ependymoma\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/supratentorial_ependymoma_yap1_fusion_positive\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8567\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0956992\nname: posterior fossa group A ependymoma\ndef: \"A posterior fossa ependymoma that arises in the posterior fossa with characteristic DNA methylation patterns, including CpG island hypermethylation, global DNA hypomethylation, reduction of nuclear H3 p.K28me3 (K27me3) expression, and EZHIP overexpression.\" [DOID:0081254]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0081254\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0026779\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C186450\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: DOID:0081254 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: GARD:0026779 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1810123 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: NCIT:C186450 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5670548 {source=\"MEDGEN:1810123\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0850339 {source=\"DOID:0081254\"} ! posterior fossa ependymoma\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/posterior_fossa_group_a_ependymoma\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8567\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0956993\nname: posterior fossa group B ependymoma\ndef: \"A posterior fossa ependymoma that arises in the posterior fossa with characteristic DNA methylation patterns including retention of nuclear H3 p.K28me3 (K27me3) expression, absence of CpG island hypermethylation, absence of global DNA hypomethylation, and absence of EZHIP overexpression.\" [DOID:0081255]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0081255\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0026780\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C186451\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: DOID:0081255 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: GARD:0026780 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: NCIT:C186451 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0850339 {source=\"DOID:0081255\"} ! posterior fossa ependymoma\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/posterior_fossa_group_b_ependymoma\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8567\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0956994\nname: astrocytoma, IDH-mutant, grade 2\ndef: \"An IDH-mutant anaplastic astrocytoma that is characterized by the presence of well-differentiated fibrillary glial cells diffusely infiltrating the central nervous system.\" [DOID:0081256]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0081256\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0026781\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C129271\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: DOID:0081256 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: GARD:0026781 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:927224 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: NCIT:C129271 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0009-0001-6494-4831\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C4289692 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:927224\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0850332 {source=\"DOID:0081256\"} ! IDH-mutant anaplastic astrocytoma\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/astrocytoma_idh_mutant_grade_2\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0956995\nname: astrocytoma, IDH-mutant, grade 3\ndef: \"An IDH-mutant anaplastic astrocytoma that is characterized by the presence of increased mitotic activity and anaplastic features.\" [DOID:0081257]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0081257\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0026782\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C129290\"}\nsubset: rare\nxre