ivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0019337 {source=\"DOID:0080841\"} ! autoimmune bullous skin disease\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/pemphigoid\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9097\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010122\nname: trichrome vitiligo\ndef: \"Any form of vitiligo characterized by a tan zone of varying width between normal and depigmented skin. This intermediate tan zone has more inflammatory cells, Langerhans cells, and melanophages than vitiliginous or normal skin. The number of melanocytes is greater than in vitiliginous skin but fewer than in normal skin.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473, PMID:21839315]\nxref: MEDGEN:697977 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: SCTID:403270009 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C1274649 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:697977\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0008661 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473\"} ! vitiligo\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8542\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010154\nname: adult hypophosphatasia\ndef: \"Adult hypophosphatasia (A-HPP) is a mildform of hypophosphatasia characterized by osteomalacia, chondrocalcinosis, osteoarthropathy, stress fractures duringmiddle age, and dental anomalies.\" [Orphanet:247676]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0110913\"}\nsubset: doid_rare {source=\"DOID:0110913\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028131\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:146300\"}\nsubset: ordo_subtype_of_a_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:247676\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:247676\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"adult hypophosphatasia\" EXACT [DOID:0110913, Orphanet:247676] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"hypophosphatasia of adults\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern, MONDO:patterns/adult]\nxref: DOID:0110913 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: GARD:0028131 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:120636 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:146300 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: Orphanet:247676 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: SCTID:20756002 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0268413 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:120636\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0018570 ! hypophosphatasia\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/hypophosphatasia_adult\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7693\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8755\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010168\nname: childhood hypophosphatasia\ndef: \"Childhood-onset hypophosphatasia is a rare, mildform of hypophosphatasia characterized by onset after six months of age and widely variable clinical features from low bone mineral density for age, to unexplained fractures,skeletal deformities,and rickets with short stature and waddling gait.\" [Orphanet:247667]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0110915\"}\nsubset: doid_rare {source=\"DOID:0110915\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028132\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:241510\"}\nsubset: ordo_subtype_of_a_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:247667\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:247667\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"childhood hypophosphatasia\" EXACT [DOID:0110915] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"childhood-onset hypophosphatasia\" RELATED [GARD:0008735]\nsynonym: \"hypophosphatasia of childhood\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern, MONDO:patterns/childhood]\nsynonym: \"pediatric hypophosphatasia\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern,